                                            </table>
                                        </div>
                                        <h2 class="ref-orig-head" data-mc-autonum="Originated in version"><span class="autonumber"><span>Originated in version</span></span>&#160;</h2>
                                        <p class="or-origin">12.0</p>
                                        <h2 class="ref-desc-head" data-mc-autonum="Description"><span class="autonumber"><span>Description</span></span>&#160;</h2>
                                        <p>Sorts the records in the current found set according to the context of a specified field, letting you create scripts that behave similarly to interactively using the shortcut menu in Table View. If you do not specify a field, the script sorts by the field that is active when the script runs. If there is no active field when the script runs, FileMaker&#160;Pro displays an invalid sort order alert.</p>
                                        <p class="tip" data-mc-autonum="&lt;b&gt;Tip &#160;&lt;/b&gt;"><span class="autonumber"><span><b>Tip &#160;</b></span></span>You can find the records you want to sort (using <a class="LinktoScriptStep MCXref xref xrefLinktoScriptStep" href="perform-find.html">Perform Find script step</a> or <a class="LinktoScriptStep MCXref xref xrefLinktoScriptStep" href="show-all-records.html">Show All Records script step</a>) before using this script step. You don''t need to use the <a class="LinktoScriptStep MCXref xref xrefLinktoScriptStep" href="enter-browse-mode.html">Enter Browse Mode script step</a> or <a class="LinktoScriptStep MCXref xref xrefLinktoScriptStep" href="go-to-record-request-page.html">Go to Record/Request/Page script step</a> after using Sort Records by Field.</p>
                                        <h2 class="ref-example1-head" data-mc-autonum="Example 1"><span class="autonumber"><span>Example 1</span></span>&#160;</h2>
                                        <p>Sorts the current found set by the active field. Can be started by the OnObjectValidate script trigger to maintain the current found set''s sort order when field values change.</p>
                                        <div class="codeSnippet"><a class="codeSnippetCopyButton" role="button" href="javascript:void(0);">Copy</a>
                                            <div class="codeSnippetBody" data-mc-use-line-numbers="False" data-mc-line-number-start="1" data-mc-continue="False"><pre><code>Sort Records by Field [Ascending]</code></pre>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <h2 class="ref-examplen-head" data-mc-autonum="Example 2"><span class="autonumber"><span>Example 2</span></span>&#160;</h2>
                                        <p>Shows invoices for the current customer ID, with the most recent invoice listed first.</p>
                                        <div class="codeSnippet"><a class="codeSnippetCopyButton" role="button" href="javascript:void(0);">Copy</a>
                                            <div class="codeSnippetBody" data-mc-use-line-numbers="False" data-mc-line-number-start="1" data-mc-continue="False"><pre><code>Find Matching Records [Replace; Invoices::Customer ID]<br />Sort Records by Field [Descending; Invoices::Invoice ID]</code></pre>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
